msgid ""
"In at most one row, `(<commit-ish>)` will appear to indicate the ref that is "
"most likely the ref used as a starting point for the branch that produced "
"_<commit-ish>_. This choice is made using a heuristic: choose the ref that "
"minimizes the number of commits in the first-parent history of _<commit-"
"ish>_ and not in the first-parent history of the ref."
msgstr ""
"指定の `<committish>` を生成したブランチの開始点として最も可能性の高い ref で"
"あると選択した1行には `(<committish>)` と表記されます。 この選択は、ヒューリ"
"スティックを使用して行われます: つまり、 `<committish>` の最初の親の履歴の中"
"でコミットの数を最小化する ref を選択します。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.adoc:202
msgid ""
"For example, consider the following figure of first-parent histories of "
"several refs:"
msgstr ""
"たとえば、 いくつかの ref の最初の親の履歴について以下の図を考えてみましょう:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.adoc:214
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*--*--*--*--*--* refs/heads/A\n"
"\\\n"
" \\\n"
"  *--*--*--* refs/heads/B\n"
"   \\     \\\n"
"    \\     \\\n"
"     *     * refs/heads/C\n"
"      \\\n"
"       \\\n"
"\t*--* refs/heads/D\n"
msgstr ""
"*--*--*--*--*--* refs/heads/A\n"
"\\\n"
" \\\n"
"  *--*--*--* refs/heads/B\n"
"   \\     \\\n"
"    \\     \\\n"
"     *     * refs/heads/C\n"
"      \\\n"
"       \\\n"
"\t*--* refs/heads/D\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.adoc:218
msgid ""
"Here, if `A`, `B`, and `C` are the filtered references, and the format "
"string is `%(refname):%(is-base:D)`, then the output would be"
msgstr ""
"ここで、 `A` と `B` と `C` がフィルタリングされた参照であり、 書式文字列が "
"`%(refname):%(is-base:D)` ならば、 出力は以下になります"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.adoc:223
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"refs/heads/A:\n"
"refs/heads/B:(D)\n"
"refs/heads/C:\n"
msgstr ""
"refs/heads/A:\n"
"refs/heads/B:(D)\n"
"refs/heads/C:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.adoc:229
msgid ""
"This is because the first-parent history of `D` has its earliest "
"intersection with the first-parent histories of the filtered refs at a "
"common first-parent ancestor of `B` and `C` and ties are broken by the "
"earliest ref in the sorted order."
msgstr ""
"これは、  `D` の最初の親の履歴は、 `B` と `C` の共通の祖先でフィルターされた "
"ref 達の最初の親の履歴との間で直近の交差を持っていて、 `B` と `C` が同列の場"
"合はソートされた順序で最も先の ref によって解決とするためです。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.adoc:233
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Note that this token will not appear if the first-parent history of "
#| "`<committish>` does not intersect the first-parent histories of the "
#| "filtered refs."
msgid ""
"Note that this token will not appear if the first-parent history of _<commit-"
"ish>_ does not intersect the first-parent histories of the filtered refs."
msgstr ""
"注意: このトークンは、 `<committish>` の最初の親の履歴がフィルターされたref達"
"の最初の親の歴史と交差していない場合には表示されないことに注意してください。"

